[ti:Anybody Still Awake?]
[ar:Ash Stu]
[al:Ash Stu, Vol. I]
[re:aligned with Demucs vocal separation + MMS forced alignment, cross-checked with Whisper alignment; edit timestamps by hand if a line is off]
[00:24.86]There used to be a brighter boy
[00:28.84]With pockets full of tinker toys
[00:33.02]Who liked to say that he could spell his name
[00:41.79]Tied the laces on his boots
[00:45.61]And scurried off to catch the bell
[00:50.09]Serenades an empty room when he is called for show and tell
[00:58.42]Shuts his eyes and tastes the clouds
[01:02.22]Alone in his hot air balloon
[01:06.74]Lifts beyond the atmosphere and starts to drift towards the moon
[01:15.07]Humming old forgotten tunes
[01:18.17]While waltzing in his own embrace
[01:23.43]Shouts from heaven down to earth, "is anybody still awake"?
